{"id": "EUVD-2026-97381", "enisaUuid": "b1b8214c-8fe5-3570-90ff-a5c2e6069e19", "description": "MoguBlog through 6.2 contains a broken access control vulnerability that allows authenticated administrators to move or rename other administrators' network-disk files by supplying their file paths. Attackers can send crafted requests to POST /networkDisk/moveFile, batchMoveFile, or edit, which update rows without admin_uid checks, relocating or renaming other users' files and folders.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T13:10:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:43:33", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/mogu_blog_v2/poc_networkDisk_ownership.py", "https://github.com/moxi624/mogu_blog_v2/blob/025d78c7ac7e19b1abf796fa3cc158d855723d15/mogu_picture/src/main/java/com/moxi/mogublog/picture/restapi/NetworkDiskRestApi.java#L165-L191", "https://github.com/moxi624/mogu_blog_v2/blob/025d78c7ac7e19b1abf796fa3cc158d855723d15/mogu_picture/src/main/java/com/moxi/mogublog/picture/service/impl/NetworkDiskServiceImpl.java#L239-L302", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mogublog-through-6.2-broken-access-control-via-networkdisk-movefile-and-edit"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109177", "GHSA-487q-jr6j-w878"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8035591c-393f-3c93-8531-896d29720ed0", "product": {"name": "MoguBlog", "vendor": {"name": "moxi624"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "887b3adc-1b93-3399-8e38-10f88c079a72", "vendor": {"name": "moxi624"}}], "isExploited": false}